CORE
main.c
--apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The assigns clause of the inner loop is inferred. The write p->f in w aliases
s.f, so the inferred write set gets the target (&s)->f, which is built from
the may-alias information. Such targets must carry a source location: the
instrumentation of the outer loop visits the checks generated for the inner
loop, and a check without a source location failed a precondition in
instrument_spec_assigns.h.
